                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "237936253",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561199196159023",
                            "num_reviews": 17,
                            "playtime_forever": 1013,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 105,
                            "playtime_at_review": 1013,
                            "last_played": 1792245937
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I genuinely had such an amazing time with this game, and was really pleasantly surprised by the quality of the writing. Each individual trauma present in each route is treated with a lot of kindness and is really thought out. I liked how each route points to clues in the overarching story, especially going through each route and seeing the echoes of other characters and their journeys without your thumb on their scale. It was such a treat! I enjoyed character tropes I'm not usually a fan of (cough cough, tsundere, cough cough, Noel). \n\nLike a different review says, and thank you for the advice, I would recommend going through Utopia's routes first, then Hell, Limbo, finding Faye, and finally [spoiler] Cheri. \n[/spoiler] \n\nThis was genuinely one of the best visual novel games that touches on the inherent meta time loop quality. The creators of this game truly made a beautiful, fleshed out world, and I want to thank Repurpose Studios sincerely for the 16 hour journey they took me on lmao. The CGs were really gorgeous, I loved the music, and the humour throughout. DJ Roadkill is such a time capsule hahaha!\n\nWithout wanting to sound naive, I really can't think of anything to warn new players about, apart from the lack of achievements (so just write down what routes you get if you're a completionist). I saw some reviews saying the prologue was a bit slow, and I wouldn't really agree. Essentially, you go through Limbo and have individual moments with (most of) the romanceables, and go through different locations to familarise yourself with Limbo's dilapidated city. You gotta meet the players before you commit to a route that playthrough! I think if you're playing visual novels, you'll enjoy the read. \n\nTruly, I would encourage you to give this game a proper go. You will be rewarded for your time into each route, and I hope you enjoy the journey as much as I did. Bless you Kickstarter backers for letting me romance Faye.",
